# Runtime governance

- Locate the owning crate before editing: contract owns public vocabulary and ports, engine
  owns governance decisions, taskmesh owns host adapters, and taskmesh-rayon owns the Rayon
  adapter.
- Read `docs/adr/0001-hexagonal-feature-sliced-architecture.md` only for crate or dependency
  boundary changes.
- For public API changes, read the relevant part of `docs/taskmesh-library-spec.md`; for wire or
  external behavior, use `docs/taskmesh-external-interface.md`.
- Run the owning crate's focused tests first. Broaden verification only when the changed
  surface crosses crate boundaries or a required gate demands it.
